# data-extraction holds source and data side by side. Track the source,
# never the data. Ignore the whole tree, then re-admit what belongs in Git.
# The directory line matters: Git will not descend into an excluded
# directory, so without it the scripts under classification_output/ and
# openalex_ng_science_2000_2026/ would stay invisible.
/01-data-engineering/data-extraction/**
!/01-data-engineering/data-extraction/**/
!/01-data-engineering/data-extraction/**/*.py
!/01-data-engineering/data-extraction/*.md
!/01-data-engineering/data-extraction/download-and-parse-pdfs.ipynb
!/01-data-engineering/data-extraction/llm-claim-extraction.ipynb
!/01-data-engineering/data-extraction/prompt-versions/README.md
!/01-data-engineering/data-extraction/prompt-versions/mufasa-extraction-2.2-candidate.2/*.md
!/01-data-engineering/data-extraction/prompt-versions/mufasa-extraction-2.2-candidate.2/*.txt
!/01-data-engineering/data-extraction/prompt-versions/mufasa-extraction-2.3-candidate.1/*.md
!/01-data-engineering/data-extraction/prompt-versions/mufasa-extraction-2.3-candidate.1/*.txt
# Re-ignore vendored dependencies. The negation above is a later rule than
# the global node_modules line, so without this it drags in every bundled
# .py from pnpm and node-gyp.
/01-data-engineering/data-extraction/**/node_modules/

# Large model, document, database, and index artifacts
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.onnx
*.pdf
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.lbug
*.index
/model/

# Tabular production artifacts. The reviewed public fixture is allowed.
*.parquet
!01-data-engineering/samples/classification-benchmark-200.parquet

# Operating-system noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
~$*

# Private working notes. Anything named *.local.md stays on the machine that
# wrote it - raw discussion, half-formed ideas, notes not meant for the repo.
*.local.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Judge-facing push. Code and results travel; corpora and weights do not.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Archives. corpus_splits.zip alone is 146 MB.
*.zip

# The Colab staging folder: parquet tables and a 153 MB markdown archive.
/upload to colab/

# Test scratch
/.test_runtime/
/.pytest_tmp_*/

# Notebooks are ignored by the data-extraction rule above; these five carry
# results a judge should be able to read without running anything.
!/01-data-engineering/data-extraction/build-training-set.ipynb
!/01-data-engineering/data-extraction/split-corpus.ipynb
!/01-data-engineering/data-extraction/prepare-citation-metadata.ipynb
!/01-data-engineering/data-extraction/sample-training-set.ipynb
!/01-data-engineering/data-extraction/production-classification.ipynb

# and the converted scripts
!/01-data-engineering/data-extraction/pipeline-scripts/
!/01-data-engineering/data-extraction/pipeline-scripts/*.py

